## Vercel Web Analytics Implementation

Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for the Capital Kranti website.

### What Was Implemented

1. **Package Installation**
   - Installed `@vercel/analytics` version 2.0.1
   - Updated package.json and package-lock.json accordingly

2. **Analytics Component Integration**
   - Added the Analytics component to all three root layout files:
     - `app/(en)/en/layout.tsx` - English version
     - `app/(gu)/layout.tsx` - Gujarati version
     - `app/(hi)/hi/layout.tsx` - Hindi version
   
3. **Implementation Details**
   - Imported `Analytics` from `@vercel/analytics/next` in each layout file
   - Added `<Analytics />` component at the end of the `<body>` tag
   - Preserved all existing code structure, fonts, and functionality
   - Followed the official Vercel documentation for Next.js App Router

### Files Modified

- `site/package.json` - Added @vercel/analytics dependency
- `site/package-lock.json` - Updated with new package dependencies
- `site/app/(en)/en/layout.tsx` - Added Analytics to English layout
- `site/app/(gu)/layout.tsx` - Added Analytics to Gujarati layout
- `site/app/(hi)/hi/layout.tsx` - Added Analytics to Hindi layout

### Verification Completed

✓ TypeScript type checking passed (`npm run typecheck`)
✓ Next.js production build successful (`npm run build`)
✓ All 198 pages compiled without errors
✓ No breaking changes to existing functionality

### Next Steps

To activate analytics:
1. Deploy this update to Vercel
2. Enable Web Analytics in the Vercel dashboard (Analytics → Enable button)
3. Analytics data will start appearing in the Vercel dashboard after deployment

### Technical Notes

- This is a multi-lingual site with separate root layouts for each language
- Analytics component was added to all three layouts to ensure tracking across all language versions
- The implementation follows Next.js App Router best practices as documented in the official Vercel quickstart guide
- The Analytics component will automatically track page views and web vitals across all routes
